{"id":"G5217","lemma":"ὑπάγω","transliteration":"hupagō","sayIt":"hupagō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to go","meaning":"ὑπ-άγω\n[in LXX: Exo.14:21 (הָלַךְ hi.), elsewhere only as seel., Tob.8:21, al. ;]\na word of the vulgar language, in Pres. and imperfect only (Bl., § 53, 1).\nI. Trans.\n1. to lead or bring under, subdue (Hom., Hdt., al.; Ex, l.with).\n2. to lead on slowly (Hdt., Xen., al.).\nII. Intrans., to go slowly away, withdraw oneself, depart (so less frequently in cl.; Thuc., Eur., al.): absol., Mat.8:32 13:44, Mrk.6:33, Luk.8:42 17:14, Jhn.6:67 8:2 11:44 14:5, 28 18:8; οἱ ἐρχόμενοι κ. οἱ ὑπάγοντες, Mrk.6:31; ὑπῆγον κ. ἐπίστευον, Jhn.12:11; ἵνα ὑπαγῆτε κ. καρπὸν ψέρητε, Jhn.15:16; opposite to ἔρχεσθαι, Jhn.3:8 8:14; imperat., ὕπαγε, Mat.4:10 8:13 20:14, Mrk.2:9 T, Mrk.7:29 10:52; εἰς εἰρήνην (ἐν εἰ.), Mrk.5:34, Jas.2:16; id. prefixed to another imperat. (Bl., § 79, 4), Mat.5:34 8:4 18:15 19:21 21:28 27:65 28:10, Mrk.1:44 10:21 16:7, Jhn.4:16 9:7, Rev.10:8; with καί inserted, Rev.16:1; euphemistically, of death, Mat.26:24, Mrk.14:21; with adv.: ποῦ (which see), Jhn.12:35 14:5 16:5, 1Jn.2:11; ὅπου (which see), Jhn.8:21-22 13:33, 36 14:4 Rev.14:4; ἐκεῖ, Jhn.11:8; with prep.: πρός, Jhn.7:33 13:3 16:5, 10 16:17; εἰς, Mat.9:6 20:4, 7, Mrk.2:11 11:2 14:13, Luk.19:30, Jhn.6:21 7:3 9:11 11:31, Rev.13:10 17:8, 11; εἰς . . . πρός, Mat.26:18, Mrk.5:19; ἐπί, Luk.12:58; μετά, Mat.5:41; ὀπίσω, Mat.16:23, Mrk.8:33; with inf., Jhn.21:3.†\n(AS)","glosses":["go","going","am going","get","am going away","away from me"],"count":75,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-4","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"Away from Me","kjv":"Get thee hence"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":24,"renderings":{"bsb":"go and","kjv":"go thy way"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":41,"renderings":{"bsb":"go","kjv":"go"}},{"chapterId":"mat-8","v":4,"renderings":{"bsb":"go","kjv":"go thy way"}},{"chapterId":"mat-8","v":13,"renderings":{"bsb":"Go","kjv":"Go thy way"}},{"chapterId":"mat-8","v":32,"rendering